translation_en:
Investigating Censor of the Shaanxi Circuit Cui Yu 崔璵, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the yichou year (1445).

Paper Receivers (受卷官):
Grand Master Exemplar and Vice Minister of the Court of Imperial Sacrifices Wang Qian 王謙, a National University Student;
Gentleman for Fostering Service and Left Admonisher of the Left Secretariat of the Heir Apparent, concurrently Historiographer of the Hanlin Academy Zhou Hongmo 周洪謨, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the yichou year (1445);
Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Rites Zhang Shi 張軾, a National University Student;
Left Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Personnel Li Zan 李讚, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the wuchen year (1448).

Sealing Officials (彌封官):
Lesser Grand Master of the Palace and Minister of the Court of Imperial Entertainments Wei Neng 蔚能;
Grand Master for Admonishment and Vice Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial Zhang Xiang 張翔, a tribute scholar (gongshi) of the renzi year (1432);
Gentleman for Fostering Service and Left Admonisher of the Left Secretariat of the Heir Apparent, concurrently Historiographer of the Hanlin Academy Liu Jun 劉俊, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the yichou year (1445);
Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Revenue Liu Wei 劉煒, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the jiwei year (1439);
Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for War Su Lin 蘇霖, a National University Student.

Paper Custodians (掌卷官):
Rectifier of the Left Secretariat of the Heir Apparent, concurrently Historiographer of the Hanlin Academy Li Tai 李泰, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the wuchen year (1448);
Gentleman for Attending to Service and Historiographer of the Hanlin Academy Wu Hui 吳匯, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the xinwei year (1451);
Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Justice Wang Zhen 王鎮, a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the yichou year (1445);
Chief Supervising Secretary of the Office of Scrutiny for Works Feng Sheng 𠗾盛 [馮盛], a metropolitan graduate (jinshi) of the wuchen year (1448).

Patrolling Officials (巡綽官):
General for Cherishing the Distant and Vice Commander of the Embroidered-Uniform Guard Bi Wang 畢旺;
General for Cherishing the Distant and Vice Commander of the Embroidered-Uniform Guard Cao Jing 曹敬.
